WASTEPAY - USER ROLES


1. RESIDENTS

Description:
Residents are individuals or households requesting plastic waste collection services.

Permissions:

- Submit home collection requests without creating an account.
- Optionally create an account to save personal information.
- View pickup request status.
- Receive SMS notifications.
- View pickup history if registered.

Restrictions:

- No access to financial or operational systems.



--------------------------------------------------


2. PLASTIC COLLECTORS

Description:
Plastic collectors are individuals who collect plastic waste and deliver it to WastePay depots.

Permissions:

- Maintain a verified collector account.
- Receive Mobile Money payments.
- View payment history.
- View collection statistics.
- Download digital payout receipts.

Business Rules:

- One verified Mobile Money number per account.
- Mobile Money number is required for payouts.



--------------------------------------------------


3. DEPOT AGENTS

Description:
Depot agents are responsible for processing plastic waste transactions.

Permissions:

- Scan plastic packaging barcodes.
- Capture verification photographs.
- Input plastic weights.
- Create payout requests.
- View personal transaction history.

Restrictions:

- Cannot approve payouts.
- Cannot modify pricing rules.
- Cannot view other agents' transactions.
- Cannot access financial analytics.



--------------------------------------------------


4. DEPOT MANAGERS

Description:
Depot managers supervise local depot operations.

Permissions:

- Approve or reject payout requests.
- Manage depot staff.
- View depot analytics.
- Monitor daily operations.
- View local transaction reports.

Restrictions:

- Cannot modify pricing rules.
- Cannot access global administrative settings.



--------------------------------------------------


5. PICKUP DRIVERS

Description:
Pickup drivers are responsible for home collection operations.

Permissions:

- Receive pickup assignments.
- Update pickup statuses.
- Capture collection photographs.
- Access Google Maps navigation links.
- Complete assigned pickup tasks.

Restrictions:

- No access to financial information.
- No access to pricing systems.



--------------------------------------------------


6. RECYCLING PROCESSORS

Description:
Recycling processors purchase and transport processed plastic inventory.

Permissions:

- View available plastic inventory.
- View plastic categories and quantities.
- Receive inventory notifications.

Restrictions:

- No access to payment information.
- No access to collector data.
- No access to administrative systems.



--------------------------------------------------


7. WASTEPAY SUPER ADMINISTRATOR

Description:
The Super Administrator maintains full control over the WastePay ecosystem.

Permissions:

- Manage all users.
- Configure pricing rules.
- Monitor Mobile Money corporate wallets.
- View nationwide analytics.
- Register new depots.
- Manage system settings.
- Manage administrator accounts.
- Access environmental impact dashboards.
- Access all financial and operational reports.

Restrictions:

- None.



--------------------------------------------------


SECURITY MODEL

Every user role is granted access only to the information and tools required for their operational responsibilities.

WastePay follows the principle of least privilege:

Users receive the minimum permissions necessary to perform their tasks securely and efficiently.